Rule 3 — Both

Both → used for two people/things.

Positive construction:
Both + A + and + B

Examples:
Both Ram and Shyam are present.
Both the students and the teacher attended the meeting.
Both of them are ready.

Subject–verb agreement:
Both → plural verb

Both of them are...
Both students were...

Important:
Both ... and ... → positive construction
Both the students as well as teacher attended.❌
Both the students and teacher attended.✅

Instead of:
Both of them did not go. ❌ (when the intended meaning is that neither went)

Use:
Neither of them went. ✅
